  "response_text": "The stack pool is a dedicated section of memory reserved for thread stacks. Since each thread needs its own stack space to store function calls, local variables, and context, the stack pool provides separate, safe memory regions for each thread\u2019s stack. In future labs, when we create multiple threads, each one will be assigned a stack from this pool, so their data won\u2019t interfere with each other. This lets the operating system run several threads at the same time safely.\\n",
